{"schema_version":"literature-map-v1","map_id":"0baabeae7268429c9f7e4de8098ae1d0","node_id":"21041260a5394f42891b020128fa60fa","analysis_id":"7c63cba835c044859c571dbc87f6a48a","job_id":"95d900a561664e8b9db4300189abf336","status":"completed","analysis":{"analysis_id":"7c63cba835c044859c571dbc87f6a48a","map_id":"0baabeae7268429c9f7e4de8098ae1d0","node_id":"21041260a5394f42891b020128fa60fa","version":1,"status":"completed","evidence_level":"abstract","source_version":"c518a10f28b2656ae30f53790a67ef835c8ebe219168460969b763f481d1e42c","model_id":"qwen3.8:27b","job_id":"95d900a561664e8b9db4300189abf336","created_at":"2026-10-20T16:23:55.600416+00:00","updated_at":"2026-10-20T16:24:33.681668+00:00","result":{"citations":[],"source_refs":[{"kind":"abstract","node_id":"21041260a5394f42891b020128fa60fa"}],"summary":"**论文标题**：Graph Attention Networks (GAT)\n\n**核心方法**：\n提出了一种基于**掩码自注意力机制（masked self-attentional layers）**的图神经网络架构。该模型通过堆叠注意力层，使节点能够对其邻居节点的特征进行加权聚合，从而隐式地为不同邻居分配不同的权重。\n\n**解决的关键问题**：\n1.  **克服谱方法局限**：避免了传统基于谱的图神经网络（Spectral GNNs）所需的昂贵矩阵运算（如矩阵求逆）。\n2.  **无需预知图结构**：不依赖于事先知道完整的图结构，因此既适用于**归纳式（inductive）**任务，也适用于**传递式（transductive）**任务。\n3.  **邻居重要性区分**：解决了传统图卷积方法中无法区分邻居节点重要性的问题。\n\n**实验验证**：\n在四个标准图基准数据集（Cora, Citeseer, Pubmed, 蛋白质-蛋白质相互作用数据集）上，GAT 模型达到了或超越了当时的最先进（SOTA）结果，并在测试图未在训练集中出现的情况下展示了良好的泛化能力。"}},"job":{"job_id":"95d900a561664e8b9db4300189abf336","map_id":"0baabeae7268429c9f7e4de8098ae1d0","operation":"analysis","status":"completed","step":"finished","cursor":{"analysis_id":"7c63cba835c044859c571dbc87f6a48a","evidence_level":"abstract","node_id":"21041260a5394f42891b020128fa60fa"},"counts":{"analysis_version":1},"failed_units":[],"created_at":"2026-10-20T16:23:55.600416+00:00","updated_at":"2026-10-20T16:24:33.681668+00:00"}}